foreign  Chapel in central France you'll find  this enigmatic Fresco it's a scene from  The Bible depicting Adam and Eve in the  Garden of Eden behind them is the tree  of knowledge except that it doesn't look  like a tree instead it looks like a  giant mushroom why could artworks like  this reveal Hidden Truths about  Christianity and psychedelics or is  there another explanation one that's  more rooted in the weird world of  medieval illustration welcome to strange  Christian art this episode psychedelics  for many years now people have noticed  mushrooms throughout religious art often  in scenes from The Bible like this one  it's from the great Canterbury Salter  with a portrait of Jesus during the  creation of Earth Below him are these  bright multicolored plants plants that  look an awful lot like fungi in fact a  cross-medieval artworks you'll seem to  find these mushrooms everywhere from  painted wood panels featuring branching  toadstools to cathedral-stained glass  with well whatever this is but the real  centerpiece is the plain Corral to  Fresco that 12th century wool painting  of the Garden of Eden it's a bizarre  image the tree of knowledge looks like a  giant mushroom from its rounded cap to  fruiting bodies growing off the stalk  some have remarked that it shares a  strong resemblance to an Amanita  mascaria a fungus that produces this  bright red Toadstool comparing the two  side by side they do indeed look very  similar even down to the red coloring  and white spots but what do these  mushrooms have to do with the biblical  story of Adam and Eve well it might have  something to do with this mushroom  having psychoactive properties aminita  mascaria contains a chemical called  muscamole when metabolized it can create  feelings of euphoria an outer body  experiences but before you get any ideas  the mushroom is also highly toxic if  handled incorrectly it can make you very  ill symptoms include nausea Tremors and  fits of muscle spasm deaths are rare 