ese  are drawings of trees rendered with  strange forms and bright colors under  close inspection there are certain  giveaways to this like the presence of  leaves  returning to the plane Corral Fresco the  tree of knowledge really is a tree  instead of stalks these are branches and  the dots are meant to resemble leaves I  know it looks strange but if you zoom in  on the steak you can see an apple in its  mouth this giant mushroom is most likely  an apple tree  given how weird some medieval plants are  drawn it makes sense how some authors  like Allegro saw magic mushrooms instead  of trees the unique shapes and colors  make them very hard to identify one  person's tree is another person's  mushroom it's a bit like this optical  illusion what do you see a rabbit or a  duck what if I rotate it a little still  the same how we interpret these pictures  gave me an idea to make some religious  art of my own using an AI I created  these images is it a tree or is it a  mushroom some of these blurry sketches  have people in them who do you see in  these paintings could this be Jesus  could this be the Virgin Mary my  favorite image the AI came up with is  this a holy mushroom person Saint fungus  I'll call him admittedly I had a bit too  much fun making these my very own  gallery of strange Christian art when a  piece of art is vague and confusing we  use our interpretation to fill in the  gap tree mushroom mushroom tree but when  this interpretation there's also  imagination from these images some are  able to construct intricate theories  involving Christianity and psychedelics  it's not a bad question by any means but  it's important to view these pictures  within their historical context okay so  there might not be psychoactive  mushrooms hidden in Christian art but I  still think it's an interesting question  after all religious art is full of  strange Visions trippy visuals and  frightening entities are there other  examples of psychedelic Christian art I  want to in